    not_duplicate_of: []  # 427c
    pr_ref:  # 427c
    description: "The nightly gate (multi-Python matrix) is RED on dev bfa589973b with one\nproduct test failing:\n\n  packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_run_behavior_map.py::\n    test_pyproject_console_script_survives_and_is_detected_wi_papag\n  AssertionError: pyproject console-script not detected as a CLI_COMMAND\n  entrypoint\n\n  1 failed, 22803 passed, 28 skipped, 17 xfailed\n\nIT PASSES LOCALLY. Run on this box against the same tree it passes in 1.04s.\nSo this is an environment-conditional failure, not a broken assertion, and\nthe environment axis the nightly varies is the Python version. The fetched\nlog reports Python 3.10; local is 3.12.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT YET. I cannot presently say WHICH legs fail, and the reason\nis filed separately as INV-libib: fetching cron/nightly/1..4 returns\nbyte-identical output (same duration to the centisecond, all reporting 3.10),\nso the resolver is handing back one leg four times. Treat \"fails on 3.10\" as\nthe leading hypothesis and NOT as measured - the honest statement is \"at\nleast one matrix leg fails this test\", and the leg cannot be named until\nINV-libib is fixed.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS. WI-papag's subject is entrypoint detection for a pyproject\nconsole-script. If that detection is version-conditional, the behavior map's\nentrypoint set is version-conditional, and entrypoints seed reachability -\nso a supply-chain or dead-code verdict could differ by interpreter with\nnothing disclosing it. That is the shape this project treats as expensive:\na silent difference in what the tool can see.\n\nFIRST STEP, cheap and available now: run this single test under 3.10 locally\n(the nightly's own matrix versions are in .woodpecker/nightly.yml) and read\nthe assertion's actual value rather than its message. If it reproduces, the\ndetector has a version-conditional dependency - likely in how the console-\nscript entry is parsed out of pyproject metadata - and the fix is in the\ndetector, not the test.\n\nNOT SWEPT: whether any OTHER nightly-only failure is masked behind the same\nresolver defect. With four legs collapsing to one log, a distinct failure on\na leg I never saw would be invisible."  # 427c
    fields:  # 427c
      statement: "A pyproject console-script must be detected as a CLI_COMMAND entrypoint on every supported Python. VIOLATED: test_pyproject_console_script_survives_and_is_detected_wi_papag fails on the nightly matrix (log reports Python 3.10) while passing locally on 3.12, so entrypoint detection differs by interpreter with nothing disclosing it."  # 427c
      root_cause: "Not yet established. The failure is environment-conditional (green locally, red on the nightly matrix) and the differing axis is the Python version. Which legs fail cannot be read today because ci-debug collapses all four matrix legs to one log (INV-libib), so the version attribution is a leading hypothesis rather than a measurement."  # 427c
- op: discuss  # 6cb1
  at: '2026-08-16T08:39:16Z'  # 6cb1
  by: agent  # 6cb1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6cb1
  clock: 2  # 6cb1
  nonce: 6cb1  # 6cb1
  message: "MEASUREMENTS THAT RESHAPE THIS ITEM (from the 08-16 01:00 UTC full-suite\ncron log at 8b55d1f4ef, fetched with the WI-zavut log tool):\n\n1. THE \"3.10-ONLY\" HYPOTHESIS IS DEAD. The full-suite container is Python\n   3.11.14 and fails the same test the same way. Not interpreter-versioned\n   in the way filed.\n\n2. THE FAILURE IS NARROWER THAN FILED. The test's FIRST assertion (the\n   pyproject script file-node survives the noise filter with entry_point\n   set) PASSES in CI — the log's failure is `assert []` on the SECOND\n   (entrypoints list). So the file-role path works; what is missing in CI\n   is the toml_config SYMBOL-concept -> entrypoints.py derivation\n   (concept_type == \"pyproject_script\" -> CLI_COMMAND/manifest_declared).\n   The gap is in that chain, under CI conditions only.\n\n3. ENVIRONMENT AXES ELIMINATED from the failing run's own install log:\n   tree-sitter-toml 0.7.0 present; tree-sitter 0.25.2 identical to the\n   local (passing) box. Grammar availability and library versions are not\n   the axis.\n\n4. TREE WINDOW. The failing tree 8b55d1f4ef is an ancestor of 4e8c47e47d,\n   where the nightly matrix passes the full suite on ALL of 3.10-3.13. The\n   window contains only PRs #364/#365/#366 — none touching toml_config.py\n   or entrypoints.py. The failure therefore stopped expressing WITHOUT its\n   mechanism being fixed. Leading hypothesis: pytest-xdist\n   ordering/collection shift (the climb PRs added tests, redistributing\n   workers) — i.e. an inter-test interaction expressed only under CI's\n   worker layout. Treat as LATENT.\n\n5. REPRO CONSTRAINTS, stated: local single-test and whole-file runs pass\n   (3.12, xdist and single-process); this box cannot run the 3.11\n   container (agent user not in the docker group). The failure has only\n   ever been observed under CI's full-suite worker layout.\n\nNEXT LEVERS, in rough order of information-per-cost: (a) INV-libib — until\nthe four nightly leg logs stop collapsing, per-leg attribution stays\nunmeasurable; (b) a CI-side probe: run test_run_behavior_map.py FIRST /\nisolated in the cron (or -p no:randomly single-worker) to split\n\"environment\" from \"ordering\"; (c) docker-group access for a faithful\ncontainer repro. Do NOT close on the current green — that is\nnon-reproduction, not evidence."  # 6cb1
