  nonce: c390  # c390
  message: "INSTALL-SET HYPOTHESIS ELIMINATED BY EXECUTION. Second owner-fired cron, on the parity tree (dev 8e913045e0): the meta-package was demonstrably installed (hypergumbo-7.0.0 wheel built and in the Successfully-installed list; 9 previously-skipped tests un-skipped, 23,012 passed vs 23,003) and the test failed IDENTICALLY. That was the last cheap hypothesis. Remaining axes, all CI-container-only: the interpreter x container interaction (nightly's 3.11 leg passes while full-suite's 3.11 container fails — so interpreter ALONE is already excluded; something about THIS pipeline's container/load remains), and pipeline-shape concurrency (full-suite runs test-all-packages CONCURRENTLY with self-tree-validation and self-claims-gate on one agent — 3x CPU oversubscription; if any analyzer timeout inside run_behavior_map is load-sensitive, the tiny toml analysis missing its budget would produce exactly this shape; nightly's matrix legs may not co-schedule the same way). INSTRUMENT SHIPPED instead of a fourth hypothesis (dev 7640dcd9d8): the failing assertion now discloses (a) the toml-config pass's run rows, (b) every pyproject-path node with kind+meta/concepts, (c) the derived entrypoint kinds — the three candidate break points (analyzer skipped / concept not emitted / conversion dropped) produce three different messages. The NEXT red cron is a mechanism reading. No further theory until that reading exists."  # c390
