- op: discuss  # 91a2
  at: '2026-08-16T19:58:52Z'  # 91a2
  by: agent  # 91a2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 91a2
  clock: 7  # 91a2
  nonce: 91a2  # 91a2
  message: "ROOT CAUSE ESTABLISHED — by the instrument, on the third owner-fired cron.\n\nTHE READING (cron at 5a9e39f94f, tree contains the self-diagnosing assert):\n  toml passes (pass, files, nodes): [('toml', 1, 3)]        <- analyzer RAN\n  pyproject-path nodes: mycli file node PRESENT with entry_point +\n    entry_role BUT NO `concepts` KEY; project node present\n  entrypoints: []                                            <- fully empty\nLocal ground truth on the same fixture: the mycli node carries\nconcepts=[pyproject_script @ config-conventions] and entrypoints contain\nBOTH (cli_command, manifest_declared) AND (main_function,\nlanguage_convention). CI had NEITHER -> concept enrichment attached\nNOTHING in that process.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. framework_patterns._PATTERN_CACHE was keyed on framework_id\nALONE while get_frameworks_dir() — half the function's input — is\npatchable. Six tests in test_framework_patterns.py patch the dir; under\nthe patch, convention ids (main-functions, config-conventions, ...) cache\nas None; the file's OWN autouse fixture (added earlier, docstring naming\nthis exact leak!) cleared the cache before each test IN THAT FILE — so the\nLAST dir-patching test in a worker left the poison for every OTHER file's\ntests on that worker. enrich_symbols then got None for every convention\npattern -> zero concepts -> zero concept-derived entrypoints -> assert [].\n\nWHY IT LOOKED LIKE EVERYTHING ELSE FIRST: expression depends on xdist\nWORKER COMPOSITION — which tests precede the victim on its worker. That\ntracked pipeline shape, not tree, interpreter, container, or install set,\nwhich is why each of those hypotheses died by experiment in turn (tree:\nfails post-climb; interpreter: nightly 3.11 leg green; install set: parity\ncron with meta installed failed identically; local: single test, whole\ncore suite, cross-package interleave all green — different worker\ncomposition).\n\nFIX (PR in flight): cache key becomes (str(get_frameworks_dir()),\nframework_id) — a patched dir caches under its own key and CANNOT shadow\nthe real patterns; poisoning is impossible by construction for the\ndir-patching shape. Regression test pins it (patched-dir Nones must not\nshadow; caching still works within the patched scope). The file-local\nfixture stays as hygiene, docstring corrected to say what it actually\nprotected.\n\nSTATUS -> pending_validation: the behavioral validation is the next\nfull-suite cron green (which also unblocks WI-zavut). Two structural\nnotes: (1) the invariant's statement should be read as \"entrypoint\ndetection must not depend on process history\" — the version-conditional\nframing died with the 3.10 hypothesis; (2) CLASS CHECK, executed:\npartial-input memoization on a patchable resolver. Surveyed core's\nmodule-global caches and lru_cache sites. ONE sibling found and FIXED in\nthe same PR: cfg.py's _MAPPING_CACHE keyed an explicit search_dir\ncorrectly but spelled the None-default as the literal 'default' while\nresolving through patchable get_cfg_nodes_dir() — same hole, no test\npatches that getter today, re-keyed on the resolved dir so none ever can.\nReviewed and left alone: discovery._looks_like_virtualenv (lru_cache on\nthe directory path — the full input), ir._known_languages_for_evidence\n(maxsize=1 over the analyzer registry, documented as stable\npost-discovery), analyzer_identity._CACHED_HASH (registry-derived)."  # 91a2
