  message: "VALIDATED — the item's own repro, re-run on the merged tree by the owner's fourth manual cron fire: ci/woodpecker/cron/full-suite SUCCESS at dev 8e69f40356 (the cache-key fix commit), where the three preceding crons on near-identical trees each failed this one test. The A/B is as clean as CI allows: same pipeline, same container, same install set as the red parity run — the only delta is the dir-keyed cache. Root cause, mechanism, elimination history, and the executed class check (cfg.py sibling fixed in the same PR) are in the previous entry. The invariant's honest restatement stands in the record: entrypoint detection must not depend on process history; it no longer does — the poisoning shape is impossible by construction and pinned by regression test."  # 8fc1
